  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A DNA molecule consists of two long polynucleotide chains composed of four types of nucleotide subunits. Each of these chains is known as a DNA chain, or a DNA strand. Hydrogen bonds between the base portions of the nucleotides hold the two chains together.</p><p>Adenine base pairs with thymine with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> hydrogen bonds and cytosine base pairs with guanine with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> hydrogen bonds.</p><p>As we know that in DNA molecule , adenine (A) always pairs with thymine (T) and cytosine (C) always pairs with guanine (G).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c5fefee2-de89-4b80-a9ac-f0e3a48e5efa.png\" style=\"width: 809px; height: 146px;\"/></p>",
